& = & \frac{1}{2} + \sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{1}{2^{n-2}\cdot\left((n-1)^2+1\right)} - \frac{1}{2^n\cdot\left((n+1)^2+1\right)}
\end{eqnarray*}The last series telescopes to $\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{10}$; thus, our our desired answer is $\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{10} = \frac{11}{10}$.

\boxed{\frac{11}{10}}

