Therefore, $G_2 G_3$ is parallel to $BC$, and $G_2 G_3$ is one-third the length of $BC$.  Likewise, $G_1 G_2$ is parallel to $AB$, and $G_1 G_2$ is one-third the length of $AB$.  Hence, triangle $G_1 G_2 G_3$ is similar to triangle $ABC$, with ratio of similarity 1/3.  The area of triangle $ABC$ is 18, so the area of triangle $G_1 G_2 G_3$ is $18 \cdot (1/3)^2 = 2$.

\boxed{2}

